============================================================
ROLE MODEL FREEZE
============================================================

Primary roles:

OWNER
ADMIN
CO_ADMIN
TRADER

Future roles must be implementable through granular RBAC capabilities.

OWNER:
Full authorized platform control.

ADMIN / CO_ADMIN:
Operational and analytical access only.

Admin/Co-Admin must NOT have access to:

- Lead Center.
- Trader credentials.
- Account financial/control administration.
- Strategy modification.
- Risk modification.
- Execution enable/disable.
- Demo/Live authorization.
- Owner Settings.
- Critical system controls.

TRADER:
Access only to the Trader's own authorized data and assigned trading accounts.

Trader must NOT have access to:

- Other traders.
- Lead Center.
- Laboratory/internal research.
- Owner Settings.
- Internal strategy controls.
- Owner H4 confirmation.
- System-wide API usage.
- Internal Supervisor authority.
- Critical system controls.

Backend authorization is authoritative.

Hiding frontend controls is NOT sufficient authorization.

